## Architecture

This project follows **Hexagonal Architecture** (Ports & Adapters), ensuring:

- **Domain isolation** - Business logic has no framework dependencies
- **Testability** - Domain can be tested without infrastructure
- **Flexibility** - Adapters can be swapped without changing domain

### Module Dependencies

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                    app                       │
│         (wires everything together)          │
└─────────────┬───────────────┬───────────────┘
              │               │
              ▼               ▼
┌─────────────────┐   ┌───────────────────────┐
│       api       │   │       adapters/*      │
│  (controllers)  │   │  (port implementations)│
└────────┬────────┘   └───────────┬───────────┘
         │                        │
         └──────────┬─────────────┘
                    │
                    ▼
          ┌─────────────────┐
          │     domain      │
          │ (business logic)│
          └─────────────────┘
```

| Module | Can Import | Cannot Import |
|--------|------------|---------------|
| `domain` | Nothing (leaf) | api, adapters, app |
| `api` | domain | adapters, app |
| `adapters/*` | domain | api, other adapters, app |
| `app` | Everything | - |

Detekt enforces these boundaries at build time.

### Domain Layer

The domain module contains pure business logic:

- **Entities** - Core business objects (immutable data classes)
- **Value Objects** - Typed wrappers using `@JvmInline value class`
- **Ports** - Interfaces defining required operations
- **Domain Services** - Business logic that spans multiple entities

```kotlin
// Value object
@JvmInline
value class UserId(val value: String)

// Entity
data class User(
    val id: UserId,
    val name: String,
    val email: String
)

// Port (interface)
interface UserRepository {
    suspend fun findById(id: UserId): User?
    suspend fun save(user: User): User
}
```

### API Layer

REST controllers that expose domain operations:

```kotlin
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/api/users")
class UserController(
    private val userRepository: UserRepository
) {
    @GetMapping("/{id}")
    suspend fun getUser(@PathVariable id: String): User? =
        userRepository.findById(UserId(id))
}
```

### Adapters Layer

Implementations of domain ports:

```kotlin
@Repository
class UserRepositoryAdapter(
    private val jpaRepository: UserJpaRepository
) : UserRepository {

    override suspend fun findById(id: UserId): User? =
        jpaRepository.findById(id.value)?.toDomain()

    override suspend fun save(user: User): User =
        jpaRepository.save(user.toEntity()).toDomain()
}
```

## Adding a New Feature

### 1. Define Domain Types

Create entities and ports in `domain/`:

```kotlin
// domain/src/main/kotlin/{package}/domain/order/Order.kt
data class Order(val id: OrderId, val items: List<OrderItem>)

// domain/src/main/kotlin/{package}/domain/order/OrderRepository.kt
interface OrderRepository {
    suspend fun findById(id: OrderId): Order?
}
```

### 2. Create API Endpoints

Add controllers in `api/`:

```kotlin
// api/src/main/kotlin/{package}/api/order/OrderController.kt
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/api/orders")
class OrderController(private val orderRepository: OrderRepository) {
    // ...
}
```

### 3. Implement Adapters

Create port implementations in `adapters/`:

```kotlin
// adapters/postgres/src/main/kotlin/{package}/adapters/postgres/OrderRepositoryAdapter.kt
@Repository
class OrderRepositoryAdapter(...) : OrderRepository {
    // ...
}
```

### 4. Wire in App

Adapters are auto-discovered via Spring component scanning.

## Scripts Reference

| Script | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| `./gradlew build` | Build all modules and run Detekt |
| `./gradlew bootRun` | Run the application |
| `./gradlew test` | Run all tests |
| `./gradlew detekt` | Run Detekt static analysis |
| `./gradlew :domain:test` | Run domain tests only |
| `./gradlew :api:test` | Run API tests only |

